The ``InterDependencies_`` of a ``DataSet`` or ``DataSetInMem`` are now frozen once the
dataset has been started, also after the measurement has completed and when loading a
started dataset, since the parameters of a dataset can not change at that point.
``dataset.description.interdeps`` is therefore a ``FrozenInterDependencies_`` for such
datasets and modifying it in place raises a ``TypeError``. Methods that return a new
object such as ``extend`` and ``remove`` continue to work, and ``FrozenInterDependencies_``
now compares equal to an ``InterDependencies_`` with the same parameters.
The ``override`` argument of ``DataSet.set_interdependencies`` is deprecated, since the
interdependencies of a started dataset are fixed and ``override`` never updated the run
description stored in the database.
